& [CanonicalRecord: IR6FinalSlices] is the processed planning authority for IR6 final work slices
  + [canonical_uuid] is de2a711c-a802-4074-90d5-781058cf0863
  + [source_manifest_uuid] is a6dfef5d-ad42-4d0e-873b-91fb593e82d2
  + [slice_surface_uuid] is 7c3b6843-80f7-42d3-9367-6293e67d2019
  + [authority_scope] is IR6 slice order, gates, expected outputs, model routing, coordination claim projection boundaries, rendezvous packet projection boundaries, mailbox carrier non-authority policy, conflict signal proof, implementation activation boundary, and forbidden live operations scope
  + [implementation_scope] is coordination mailbox and claim projection prototype planning plus gated implementation activation
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/FSC2_Planning_Coordination_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/coordination/Coordination_Claim_And_Rendezvous_Contracts.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/FSC4_Surface_Projection_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/FSC5_Operations_Safety_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/IR5_Surface_Projection_Prototype_Implementation_Proof_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/reviews/IR5_Implementation_Completion_Review.v1.sop

  = must: use docs/slices/IR6_Final_Slices.v1.sop as the current IR6 slice surface
  = must: execute IR6-S01 first
  = must: run completion review after each IR6 slice before opening the next gated slice
  = must: keep coordination claims, rendezvous packets, mailbox messages, IRC logs, Matrix events, web events, terminal output, Codex state, Langflow diagrams, generated projections, and generated reports non-authoritative
  - never: treat IR6 slices as permission for agent dispatch, mailbox transport implementation, chat adapter implementation, dependency installation, operations simulator implementation, operations control, or live machine control

& [CanonicalIR6SliceSet] is the final IR6 slice sequence
  + [slice] is IR6-S01 coordination boundary import and invariant reconciliation
  + [slice] is IR6-S02 claim identity and work-boundary projection contract
  + [slice] is IR6-S03 rendezvous packet and mailbox carrier projection contract
  + [slice] is IR6-S04 conflict, stale-claim, and human-override review contract
  + [slice] is IR6-S05 coordination mailbox fixture plan and expected ledger plan
  + [slice] is IR6-S06 coordination mailbox projection prototype implementation plan and generated-output boundary
  + [slice] is IR6-S07 IR6 completion review and implementation activation pack

  = must: preserve this order unless completion review rebakes IR6

& [CanonicalIR6ExecutionGate] is the activation rule for IR6
  + [current_ready_slice] is IR6-S01
  + [gated_slice] is IR6-S02 until IR6-S01 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR6-S03 until IR6-S02 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR6-S04 until IR6-S03 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR6-S05 until IR6-S04 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR6-S06 until IR6-S05 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR6-S07 until IR6-S06 accepted
  + [completion_gate] is IR6 implementation activation pack accepted after IR6-S07

& [CanonicalIR6ModelRouting] is the model-routing record
  + [IR6-S01] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR6-S02] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR6-S03] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR6-S04] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR6-S05] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after IR6-S01 through IR6-S04 acceptance
  + [IR6-S06] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR6-S07] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: keep identity semantics, contested claim policy, mailbox carrier authority, human override, and final activation under deeper reasoning
  = must: treat bounded fixture planning as Spark-suitable only after claim, rendezvous, mailbox, and conflict contracts are accepted

